Z||000002||theogre||05-20-99||07:11 AM||||always shop local dealers, scrappers, and retailers, for parts before getting them online.<p>also visit  <A HREF="http://www.suspesion.com" TARGET=_blank>www.suspesion.com</A>  when you do the suspension
Z||000003||87FieroGT||05-20-99||03:26 PM||||Welcome to the family. What year is your Fiero. Like most Fiero enthusiast I do the work myself. The best thing to do about buying parts is to shop around. Don't get anxious and try to buy the first thing you see. Sometimes the dealership is cheaper and sometimes not. You will find the best price if you look hard. One of the easiest yet hardest thing to do is find a Fiero that is in a junk yard and pull the parts off of it. But they usually get crushed. 
Z||000004||Carrolles||05-20-99||03:56 PM||||If it is an 84 through 87 and you only need to replace brake pads and maybe rebuild the calipers, AutoZone's prices aren't any different than most other GM cars.<p>Good luck,<br>Carroll
